flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the pager works
    accDescr: GitHub sends the events of the GitHub App to the Worker on Cloudflare, signed with the secret of its webhook. The rules decide what needs Dennis; everything else ends there. What counts becomes one message in Telegram, edited in place as it changes, with buttons. A button runs an action of the allowlist on GitHub, such as merging a green release. Drafts, fixes and free text go to the workflow of the private control repository, which runs Claude Code with Dennis's subscription and sends its answer back, signed, as a draft, a note or a proposal that a button has to approve.

    github["`**GitHub** sends the events of the app, signed`"]
    rules{"`**The rules** of the Worker: does it need Dennis?`"}
    quiet["`No: it ends here, without a message`"]
    message["`**One message** in Telegram, edited in place as the thing changes`"]
    dennis["Dennis presses a button or writes a text"]
    action["`**An action of the allowlist** on GitHub, such as merging a green release`"]
    control["`**The private control repository** drafts a reply, starts a fix or reads the free text, with Claude Code and Dennis's subscription`"]

    github --> rules
    rules --> quiet
    rules --> message --> dennis
    dennis --> action
    dennis --> control
    control -- "a draft, a note or a proposal, signed" --> message

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class dennis you
    class github,rules,message,control bot
    class quiet,action done
